The `stderr()` metric computes clustered standard errors via the `cluster` parameter. You can specify this parameter when defining your task to cluster the standard errors on a specific variable, such as "category" metadata. For example:

```python
@task
def gpqa():
    return Task(
        dataset=read_gpqa_dataset("gpqa_main.csv"),
        solver=[
            system_message(SYSTEM_MESSAGE),
            multiple_choice(),
        ],
        scorer=choice(),
        metrics=[accuracy(), stderr(cluster="category")]
    )
```

This configuration will compute the standard error of the mean, clustered by the "category" variable. [P0458]

